|~ `::excerpt`, the kind of the facts a host tells of a failure past its
   rooms, and what is declared under it: its laws.
   The rules it holds: [QSPRN#excerpt], [QSERR#alert]. ~|

:excerpt
  |~~ An excerpt tells the facts of a failure a host prints past the room
      of a fact, under the tag of its refusal,
      `::number/add/AddendKindNotTakenError::excerpt{…}`: each fact
      whole within three hundred characters, and past them the cell the
      host keeps it in, `:addend/found ::cell"…"`, beside its tag and the
      views the kind of the fact reveals that fit the room, each under the
      name of the fact and its own, `:addend/found/tag ::vec` and
      `:addend/found/count 3410`, and beside its parts, each by the same
      rule under the name of the fact and its own: a map by its keys, an
      error at rest and an excerpt by their facts, and a value under a tag
      its kind does not wire by the parts of what it holds, whose tag stands
      under `payload/tag`, `:answer/payload/tag`; a vector, a set, a string,
      a quote and a doc stand as their views. A key is the chain a reader
      types, `:answer/addend/found/count` read as
      `::cell"…" | answer | addend | found | count`, and a host that keeps
      no cell shows the tag, the views and the parts alone. Nothing is cut:
      a fact stands whole, as a cell that gives it back whole, or as the
      facts its kind reveals of it.

      An excerpt is a map under its tag, read by its keys, and the kind of
      the refusal over it reads its facts by their names, a cell standing
      for any fact; `raise` refuses it, a failure told and not held. The
      whole is read live, a fact of a failure by `!|` and a cell by
      `answer`.
      ::link~(::kind/reveals) ::link~(::cell)
      ::link~(::qlang/hosts)
  ~~|
  ::kind
    | accepts |~~ The facts told, whole, as cells or as views. ~~| ::map
    | throws :PayloadKindNotTakenError
        |~~ An excerpt is the map of the facts a host tells of a failure,
            `::excerpt{:addend/found ::cell"…" :addend/found/count 3410}`.
        ~~|
    | proves :PayloadKindNotTakenError/refusesAVector
        |~~ An excerpt is a map of facts, no vector. ~~|
        ~(::excerpt[1] !| tag | eq ::excerpt/PayloadKindNotTakenError)
    | proves :readsBackAsItself
        |~~ An excerpt prints and reads back as itself. ~~|
        ~(::excerpt{:addend/found ::cell"f410f1df625c" :addend/found/count 3410} | eq (print | parse | answer))
    | proves :readsAViewByItsKey
        |~~ A view stands under the name of its fact and its own. ~~|
        ~(::excerpt{:addend/found/count 3410} | get /:addend/found/count | eq 3410);
